{title: Now Thank We All Our God}
{artist: Martin Rinkart · tr. Catherine Winkworth}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
Now [F]thank we [C]all our [Dm]God with [Bb]heart and [C]hands and [F]voices,
who wondrous [C]things hath [Dm]done, in [Bb]whom his [C]world re[F]joices;
who [F]from our [Bb]mothers' [C]arms hath [Dm]blessed us [C]on our [F]way
with [Bb]countless [F]gifts of [C]love, and [Dm]still is [C]ours to[F]day.

Verse 2
O [F]may this [C]bounteous God [Dm]through all [Bb]our life [C]be near [F]us,
With ever [C]joyful hearts [Dm]and blessed [Bb]peace to [C]cheer [F]us;
And [F]keep us [Bb]in [C]His grace, [Dm]and guide [C]us when [F]perplexed;
And [Bb]free [F]us from all [C]ills, in [Dm]this world and [C]the [F]next!

Verse 3
All [F]praise and [C]thanks to God [Bb]the Father [C]now be [F]given;
The Son [C]and Him [Dm]Who reigns with [Bb]Them in [C]highest [F]Heaven;
The [F]one eternal [C]God, Whom [Dm]earth [C]and Heav'n [F]adore;
For [Bb]thus [F]it was, [C]is now, [Dm]and shall [C]be [F]evermore.
